rrs[0].Field)"," \t\t})"," \t}"," }"],"additions":14,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/constants/constants.go","lines":["@@ -470,19 +470,20 @@ const ("," \t// Set to \"true\" on an LLMInferenceService to inject the middleware."," \tLLMServedByAnnotationKey = \"serving.kserve.io/enable-served-by-header\""," ","-\t// LLMDisaggregatedSetAnnotationKey opts a disaggregated (prefill/decode)","-\t// LLMInferenceService into the DisaggregatedSet workload backend, which manages","-\t// both roles as one object so they roll together during an upgrade instead of","-\t// racing independently.","+\t// LLMDisaggregatedSetAnnotationKey selects the DisaggregatedSet workload backend for","+\t// a disaggregated (prefill/decode) LLMInferenceService, which manages both roles as","+\t// one object so they roll together during an upgrade instead of racing independently."," \t//","-\t// Set on the object's metadata, not spec.annotations, since the latter propagate to","-\t// pods. The only accepted values are \"true\" and \"false\", compared case-insensitively","-\t// after trimming, matching StopAnnotationKey; anything else is rejected at admission.","+\t// It is read from spec.annotations after presets are merged. The P/D presets set it","+\t// to \"true\", so DisaggregatedSet is the default; a service sets it to \"false\" in its","+\t// own spec.annotations to keep using Deployments or LeaderWorkerSets. The only","+\t// accepted values are \"true\" and \"false\", compared case-insensitively after trimming,","+\t// matching StopAnnotationKey; anything else is rejected at admission."," \t//","-\t// Opting in additionally requires the DisaggregatedSet feature gate in the \"llmisvc\"","-\t// key of inferenceservice-config and the LWS DisaggregatedSet CRD on the cluster.","-\t// Without either, the annotation is inert and the service keeps using the Deployment","-\t// or LeaderWorkerSet path unchanged.","+\t// Using the backend additionally requires the DisaggregatedSet feature gate in the","+\t// \"llmisvc\" key of inferenceservice-config and the LWS DisaggregatedSet CRD on the","+\t// cluster. Without either, the annotation is inert and the service keeps using the","+\t// Deployment or LeaderWorkerSet path unchanged."," \tLLMDisaggregatedSetAnnotationKey = KServeAPIGroupName + \"/enable-disaggregated-set\""," "," \t// LLMAcceleratorAnnotationKey is the Status.Annotations key where the"],"additions":12,"deletions":11,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/controller/v1alpha2/llmisvc/config_loader.go","lines":["@@ -98,9 +98,13 @@ type FeatureGates struct {"," \t// (prefill/decode) services, which upgrades both roles as one coordinated unit"," \t// instead of letting them roll independently."," \t//","-\t// This gate alone changes nothing. A service opts in individually with the","-\t// serving.kserve.io/enable-disaggregated-set annotation, and the LWS","-\t// DisaggregatedSet CRD must be installed on the cluster.","+\t// The P/D presets set serving.kserve.io/enable-disaggregated-set to \"true\" in","+\t// spec.annotations, so turning the gate on moves every P/D service that does not set","+\t// it to \"false\" onto a DisaggregatedSet, provided the LWS DisaggregatedSet CRD is","+\t// installed. A running service that moves is unavailable until its new pods are","+\t// ready, and gets a MigratingToDisaggregatedSet warning event. Services pinned to","+\t// presets from an earlier release (see LLM_INFERENCE_SERVICE_CONFIG_PREFIX) do not","+\t// carry the default and keep their workloads unless they set the annotation."," \tDisaggregatedSet bool `json:\"disaggregatedSet,omitempty\"`"," }"," "],"additions":7,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"pkg/controller/v1alpha2/llmisvc/config_presets_test.go","lines":["@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@ import ("," \t\"k8s.io/utils/ptr\""," \t\"sigs.k8s.io/yaml\""," ","+\t\"github.com/kserve/kserve/pkg/constants\""," \t\"github.com/kserve/kserve/pkg/controller/v1alpha2/llmisvc\""," "," \tkservetesting \"github.com/kserve/ks